title: Kamla_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

The morning light filters through their small window.

Raju chooses to help his mother prepare for her work at the wealthy households.

Instead of rushing off to cricket practice.

He knows Kamla works incredibly hard to support their family.

The modest single room comes alive with soft golden light of dawn.

He watches his mother prepare for another day of labor.

In the homes of people who live in a completely different world.

Her movements carry the practiced efficiency of someone who maximizes every moment.

Her weathered hands sort through cleaning supplies and prepare tiffin containers.

With the quiet dignity of a woman who takes pride in honest work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Raju, beta, before you run off with that cricket bat, come help your mother.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: I need you to carry these tiffins and laundry up to the big building today.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: The High-Rise Condos?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: But Ma, that's where all the rich kids live.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: What if someone sees me carrying laundry?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Yes, beta, they live in those tall buildings and look down on people like us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: But they also pay me so we can eat.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: So you can go to school.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: So your cricket dreams might someday become possible.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Responsibility comes before play, always.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Those people in their fine apartments need us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Even if they don't always show respect.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: And we need their money to survive.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: There's no shame in honest work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Only in laziness or pride that makes us too good for the work that feeds us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I understand, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I'll help you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: And I'll be respectful, no matter how they treat us.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Remember, beta, when we're in their world, we're respectful and quiet.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: But we never bow our heads in shame.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: We work with dignity because our work has value.

<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Who's this? Another servant boy?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: I hope he's more careful than the last one who broke my mother's vase.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I'm not a servant.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: I'm just helping my mother.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: There's nothing wrong with helping family.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Helping? Is that what poor people call working for money?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Don't break anything, slum boy.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Aryan" Angry>>
Aryan: Everything here costs more than your family makes in a month.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Young master, my son is here to learn about different kinds of work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: He'll be very careful with your family's belongings.

<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Ignore words like that, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: People who talk down to others usually do it because they're insecure.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: About their own worth.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Our struggles have taught us things that boy will never understand.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju and his mother walk home from the high-rise complex, they carry the day's wages.

Earned through dignity and hard work.

Raju carries not just their meager earnings.

But a deeper understanding of social forces.

Forces that judge people by economic circumstances rather than character.

Kamla's quiet strength in the face of casual cruelty has taught him something valuable.

About maintaining self-respect in a world that often offers little respect in return.

<<set $Kamla_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===
title: Kamla_Day2
tags: 
position: -75,-229
---

<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

After yesterday's difficult encounter at the wealthy apartment, Raju chooses to spend the evening at home.

With his mother instead of going out to play cricket with friends.

The familiar warmth of their small home welcomes Raju.

As he settles beside his mother for conversation.

Rather than rushing off to evening cricket practice.

His mind still processing yesterday's exposure to casual cruelty.

That often accompanies wealth and privilege.

The simple comfort of being in a space where his worth is never questioned.

Creates a stark contrast to the hostile environment of the high-rise complex.

Kamla's presence radiates the unconditional love and support.

That anchors his sense of self.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Ma, why did that boy Aryan talk to us like that?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Just because his family has money, does he really think he's better than us?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Beta, people like Aryan live in tall buildings.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: But that doesn't mean they see far.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: They look down on us not because we're less than them.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: But because looking down makes them feel taller.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: But here's what I noticed yesterday, and what that rich boy didn't see.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You held your head high.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: When he insulted you, you didn't cower or accept his words as truth.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You stood up for yourself and for our family with dignity.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I want to prove him wrong, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: One day, when I'm successful - maybe through cricket, maybe through something else.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I want him to know that being from the slums doesn't make someone less worthy of respect.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: And you will prove him wrong, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: But not by becoming like him - dismissive and cruel.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You'll prove him wrong by being exactly who you are.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Kind, determined, and respectful to everyone regardless of their circumstances.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I see how serious you are about everything you do, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Even if your father worries about your cricket dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Even if he doesn't say it out loud yet, I want you to know.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I believe in you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Really, Ma?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: You believe I can make something of myself, even coming from here?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Beta, I've cleaned the houses of wealthy people for years.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I've seen their children - given everything, handed opportunities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Never having to work for anything.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: And then I watch you - creating your own opportunities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Working twice as hard for half the recognition.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Which child do you think is really stronger?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I'll support your dreams, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Quietly, because your father needs time to understand, but always.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: When you succeed - and I believe you will.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: It won't be because someone gave you advantages.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: It will be because you earned every step forward.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Thank you, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I promise I won't let you down.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I'll make our family proud.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju prepares for sleep with his mother's words of support echoing in his heart, he understands something important.

He has received something more valuable than any expensive equipment or coaching.

The unwavering faith of someone who knows his character intimately.

And believes in his potential despite all external obstacles.

Her promise of quiet but constant support provides a foundation of confidence.

That will sustain him through future challenges and rejections.

