title: Kamla_Revelation
tags:
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>

After three days of voluntarily helping his mother and demonstrating growing maturity, Raju accompanies Kamla to the wealthy Mehta household.

Witnessing the stark contrast between their poverty and others' abundance.

<<SetBGSprite WellingtonEstate>>

The opulent Mehta household stands as a monument to wealth and privilege.

As Raju accompanies his mother into a world where single decorative items cost more than his family's monthly income.

The stark contrast forces him to confront the economic realities that shape their daily struggles.

Kamla's practiced efficiency in navigating this environment of casual luxury reveals the dignity she maintains.

While working in spaces that emphasize their social and economic marginalization.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Watch carefully, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: See how much work it takes to earn twenty rupees?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: It seems like so much work for so little money, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Your hands are hurting.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: This is why education matters, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: So you don't spend your life cleaning other people's houses.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Watching your hands age before their time.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: While their children play with toys that cost more than our monthly food budget.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: But what about cricket, Ma?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Can't that also help us? If I get really good, maybe...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Cricket is a dream, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Dreams are beautiful.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: And after watching how serious you've been these past few days.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I'm starting to think maybe some dreams aren't as impossible as I thought.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: But we need practical plans too.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: The difference is, I can see now that you understand responsibility.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You've helped me every morning without complaining.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Even when I know you wanted to be practicing cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: That tells me maybe you can balance both dreams and reality.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I can, Ma. I can do both.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I can help you and still chase my cricket dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Then prove it.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Show me that your cricket makes you more responsible, not less.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Show me that dreams can make you stronger, not weaker.

<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju and Kamla walk home from the Mehta household with new understanding, something has shifted.

Of both the challenges they face and the possibilities that determined effort might create.

The conversation has transformed from cautious skepticism about cricket dreams.

Into conditional support based on demonstrated character.

The exposure to extreme wealth has clarified the stakes involved.

While Raju's consistent responsibility has earned him the chance to prove something important.

That athletic ambition and family duty can indeed strengthen each other.

