<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Kamla_Day5
tags:
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite LocalMarket>>

After four days of witnessing his growing maturity and dedication, Raju accompanies his mother to the local market.

Wanting to help with shopping and understand how their limited money must be stretched.

The bustling local market surrounds Raju and Kamla with the familiar sounds and smells of their neighborhood.

As they navigate between vendors hawking vegetables, household goods, and various necessities.

That must be carefully budgeted against their limited resources.

Each purchase decision reflects the harsh mathematics of poverty.

Where every rupee spent on one need means another need goes unmet.

Though today's shopping trip carries the anticipation of a significant moment.

That neither fully expects.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Excited">>
Kamla: Beta, look at this.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Excited">>
Kamla: A real cricket ball - leather, proper stitching.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Excited">>
Kamla: Not like those tennis balls you've been practicing with.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vendor" "Excited">>
Vendor: Madam, that's excellent quality - genuine leather, regulation weight.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vendor" "Excited">>
Vendor: Your son would practice like a real cricketer with that ball.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vendor" "Excited">>
Vendor: Only fifteen rupees, a very good price.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Fifteen rupees...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: That's my lunch money for three days.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: That's vegetables for the family for two days.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: That's...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Ma, please don't.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: I can keep practicing with the old tennis ball.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: It's been working fine.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: We need that money for food, for the house, for important things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Important things, you said.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Tell me, beta - after watching you for four days.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: After seeing how seriously you take both your responsibilities and your cricket practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Isn't your development important too?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: No, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: If you're going to practice cricket seriously.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: If you're going to chase this dream with the dedication you've been showing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Then you should practice with proper equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Dreams deserve proper tools.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vendor" "Smiling">>
Vendor: Your son is very lucky to have a mother who supports his games.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Vendor" "Smiling">>
Vendor: This ball will last for years with proper care.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Ma, you didn't have to do this.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I know what fifteen rupees means to our family.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I know what you're giving up.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Beta, a mother doesn't just feed her child's body.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: She feeds his dreams, his potential, his belief in himself.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: This ball isn't just for cricket practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: It's my way of saying I believe in you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: But remember this moment, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Remember what this ball represents.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: It cost me three days of meals.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: But I chose to invest in your future instead.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Serious">>
Kamla: Use it wisely. Practice with purpose.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I'll treasure this ball, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I'll use it to become the best cricketer I can be.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: And I'll make you proud - not just in cricket, but in everything I do.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You already make me proud, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Every day when you help with chores without being asked.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Every day when you balance your dreams with your responsibilities.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You're already the success I hoped you'd become.

<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As Raju and Kamla walk home from the market, the precious cricket ball represents far more than sporting equipment.

It embodies a mother's faith, sacrifice, and investment in her son's dreams.

Despite their desperate circumstances.

The weight of her trust and the magnitude of her sacrifice settle into Raju's consciousness.

Transforming the leather ball into a sacred object.

That carries the responsibility to honor both her belief and the family resources invested in his potential.

