title: Kamla_Day6
tags:
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>

After an especially successful cricket practice session with the new ball, Raju comes home directly.

Instead of playing additional games.

Excited to share his progress with Kamla.

The familiar warmth of home welcomes Raju as he returns from cricket practice.

Glowing with the excitement of someone whose efforts have produced tangible results.

His eagerness to share his progress with Kamla reflects the deepened bond.

That has developed through days of mutual support and understanding.

The cricket ball that cost his mother three days of meals has already begun to justify her investment.

Through improvements that validate both his talent and her faith in his potential.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Look at that smile, beta!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: How was practice today?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You look like you conquered the entire cricket field.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Ma, it was incredible!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Using the proper cricket ball made such a difference.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I hit six boundaries today - clean, powerful shots.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That went exactly where I aimed them.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: And I took three wickets when I was bowling!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Quizzical">>
Kamla: Six boundaries and three wickets...

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Quizzical">>
Kamla: Beta, I've heard these terms, but explain to me exactly what they mean.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Quizzical">>
Kamla: I want to understand your cricket properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Taking wickets means I bowled so well that I got the batsmen out!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: And boundaries are when you hit the ball so hard and so precisely.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That it reaches the edge of the field and you automatically get four runs!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Beta, you absolutely light up when you talk about cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I've never seen you this alive, this energetic about anything else.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: That's because cricket makes me feel... like I can be somebody special, Ma.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Like I'm not just another poor kid from the slums.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: When I'm playing, I feel like I could become someone important.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Listen to me carefully, Raju.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: You already are somebody special. You always have been.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Cricket doesn't make you special, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Cricket just gives the world a way to see the specialness that was already inside you.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: So you really believe in my cricket dreams now?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: You think they could become real?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I believe in you, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: I believe in your character, your work ethic, your dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: And your ability to make them reality while staying true to who you are.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Kamla" "Smiling">>
Kamla: Cricket is just one way that might happen.

<<HideAllCharacters>>

As the conversation about cricket success transitions into deeper affirmations, both mother and son understand something.

That something fundamental has shifted in their relationship.

From cautious support to wholehearted belief.

In possibilities that once seemed impossibly distant.

The investment in the cricket ball has already paid dividends.

In confidence and performance.

Validating Kamla's decision to sacrifice immediate needs for long-term potential.

